        "story-1": {
          "type": "story_row",
          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "how it started",
            "heading": "One Small Classroom, One Big Idea",
            "body": "<p>The sky can be bubblegum colored and horses can be bluish-orangey-green. For kids, imagination comes in all sorts of colors — most of which aren't in a box set.</p><p>Thirty-seven years ago, Tina — an enterprising full-time mom and part-time preschool teacher — never shied away from getting out the paints and messy art materials. But she noticed that when it came to creative playtime, she was the exception, not the rule. So she invented a new, mess-free way for kids to dip into all the colors of their imagination: a special dot paint applicator.</p><p>Children could layer and blend colors like never before — fill big spaces, make shapes, create textures. Kids loved the new art medium. Parents and teachers loved the finished projects, and the easy setup and cleanup even more.</p>",
            "pullquote": "We help kids create their own colors, so they can express themselves freely.",
            "pullquote_attribution": "— the Do-A-Dot Art! story",
            "reverse": false
          }
        },
        "story-2": {
          "type": "story_row",
          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "how it's going",
            "heading": "Same family. Same idea. A bigger craft closet.",
            "body": "<p>Tina didn't let her idea live only within the walls of her preschool. Along with her husband Rob, she built the original dot art marker from a creative tool for kids into an educational staple used in classrooms everywhere — and to this day, mess-free painting for kids is revolutionary.</p><p>Do-A-Dot Art! is still a family-run business, with the second generation carrying it forward. In 2026 the craft closet is growing — chunky crayons, mess-free watercolors, and more new tools, all built on the same idea Tina started with.</p><p>And we're proud of how our sets come together: assembled with love and care by a dedicated team at a special-needs work center whose work ethic and attention to detail set the standard.</p>",
            "pullquote": "Together, let's add more color to our world.",
            "pullquote_attribution": "— the Do-A-Dot Art! family",
            "reverse": true
          }
        },
